{"type":"proposition","type_name":"Proposition","number":"24.5.2","title":"SIMEX in the linear model","title_html":"SIMEX in the linear model","html":"<p>Assume the conditions of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"thm-eiv-attenuation\">@thm-eiv-attenuation</span>(c), with\none mismeasured scalar regressor of error variance <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\sigma_u^2\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msubsup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.247em; margin-left: 0;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 0.297em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D462 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, and fix <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\zeta\\ge0\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D701 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2265\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. For each <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"b\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=